Hi,
I am Akhil Vij, a masters student from IIIT-Hyderabad, India. I am
interested to work with the R project for GSOC - 2012. I am currently
pursuing MS by research program in the Center for Visual Information
Technology (CVIT)  research center at IIIT. After going through the R
repository, I felt that R is missing a compact and well-documented
package comprising of  basic Pattern Recognition (PR) methods. Several
such packages exist for matlab and other languages. This is just a
tentative list of methods we can include in the R-PR package. This
list may get extended or shortened, as I am currently in the process
of searching more existing toolboxes and exploring other R packages.

Any advice/opinions about the proposal would be highly appreciated.
Based on the opinions, I will start preparing a more detailed
proposal.

Module 1 : Linear Discriminant Functions :   Linear Classifier and its
multi-class version

Perceptron Algorithm and its multi-class version

Kozinec's Algorithm

Module 2 : Feature Extraction :                   PCA and its
kernelized version
                                                                LDA
and its kernelized version
                                                                Greedy
kernel PCA algorithm
                                                                Other
basic dimensionality reduction techniques

Module 3 : Density Estimation :                 Gaussian distribution
and Gaussion Mixture Model(GMM)
                                                               Maximum
Likelihood estimation of GMM
                                                               Minimax
Estimation
                                                               Reduced
Set Density Estimator

Module 4 : Support Vector machines :         SVMs and its variations
(like binary SVM, SMO, multi-class version)

Module 5 : Solving Pre-image Problem :       By Schoelkopf's fixed-
point algo
                                                                 By
Gradient Optimization
                                                                 By
Kwok-Tsang's algorithm

Module 6 :                                                  Reduced
Set Method for RBF Kernel
                                                                 Other
basic PR algorithms which I missed

References:

STPRTool is a popular statistical Pattern Recognition Toolbox for
matlab.
        http://cmp.felk.cvut.cz/cmp/software/stprtool/index.html

NETLAB toolbox which mainly has Neural networks and classical PR
methods.
        http://www.mathworks.com/matlabcentral/fileexchange/2654-netlab

PRtools is another widely used matlab toolbox for Pattern Recognition.
        http://www.prtools.org

Thanks,
Akhil Vij

